  "historyUrl": "https://hayday.fandom.com/wiki/Town?action=history",
  "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\"><p><br>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/e/e6/Town_Hall.png/revision/latest?cb=20191026015915\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"The Town Hall\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"The Town Hall\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/e/e6/Town_Hall.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/200?cb=20191026015915\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" class=\"mw-file-element\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Town Hall</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The <b>town</b> is a game feature which gives players a new area to play in and the opportunity to gain <a href=\"/wiki/coin-6079\" title=\"Coin\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">coins</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/experience-19023\" title=\"Experience\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">experience</a> points, and <a href=\"/wiki/reputation-14275\" title=\"Reputation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">reputation</a> points by filling <a href=\"/wiki/town-visitors-13241\" title=\"Town Visitors\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">town visitors</a>' orders.\n</p><p>It can be unlocked at <a href=\"/wiki/experience-19023\" title=\"Experience\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">experience</a> level 34 by repairing the <a href=\"/wiki/train-station-13239\" title=\"Train Station\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">train station</a> located on the <a href=\"/wiki/farm-15139\" title=\"Farm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">farm</a>.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/reputation-14275\" title=\"Reputation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">reputation</a> level 3 and up, it lets players interact with the <a href=\"/wiki/sanctuary-28458\" title=\"Sanctuary\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">sanctuary</a>.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\"><a href=\"/unavailable-source?media=File%3AGame_Soundtrack_Town.ogg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://hayday.fandom.com/wiki/File:Game_Soundtrack_Town.ogg</a></span>\n</p>\n<div></div>\n<hr>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\"><b>Going to the town</b></span></h3>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/1/16/Farm_Train_Station_Locked.png/revision/latest?cb=20150712184204\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"The broken train station\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"The broken train station\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/1/16/Farm_Train_Station_Locked.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/150?cb=20150712184204\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The broken train station</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Repairing the farm's train station costs 20,000 <a href=\"/wiki/coin-6079\" title=\"Coin\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">coins</a>, takes 5 minutes (or 10 <a href=\"/wiki/diamond-2524\" title=\"Diamond\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">diamonds</a>) and awards 39 <a href=\"/wiki/experience-19023\" title=\"Experience\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">experience</a> points. After taking the handcar to go to the town players must repair the town's <a href=\"/wiki/train-station-13239\" title=\"Train Station\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">train station</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/town-hall-13238\" title=\"Town Hall\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Town Hall</a>. It is free to repair these.\n</p>\n<div></div>\n<hr>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\"><b>Town buildings</b></span></h3>\n<p>There are several buildings in the town&#160;(see the map below):\n</p>\n<ul><li>the Eggspress train which brings <a href=\"/wiki/town-visitors-13241\" title=\"Town Visitors\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">visitors</a> to the town</li>\n<li>the <a href=\"/wiki/train-station-13239\" title=\"Train Station\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">train station</a> to allow more visitors in the town</li>\n<li>the <a href=\"/wiki/town-hall-13238\" title=\"Town Hall\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Town Hall</a> to keep track of visitors</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/service-buildings-24540\" title=\"Service Buildings\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">service buildings</a> to fill visitors' orders</li>\n<li>the <a href=\"/wiki/personal-train-13479\" title=\"Personal Train\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">personal train</a> to pick up visitors from your <a href=\"/wiki/neighborhood-10438\" title=\"Neighborhood\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">neighborhood</a></li>\n<li>the book stand and the <a href=\"/wiki/sanctuary-28458\" title=\"Sanctuary\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">sanctuary</a> on the far right (not shown on the map)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/category%2Fcategory-animal-shelters-6565\" title=\"Category:Animal Shelters\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">animal shelters</a> for <a href=\"/wiki/category%2Fcategory-sanctuary-animals-28587\" title=\"Category:Sanctuary Animals\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">sanctuary animals</a></li>\n<li>the handcar to go back to the <a href=\"/wiki/farm-15139\" title=\"Farm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">farm</a></li></ul>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/9/96/Town_Map.png/revision/latest?cb=20151026231517\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Town Map\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Town Map\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/9/96/Town_Map.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/500?cb=20151026231517\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"500\" height=\"389\" class=\"mw-file-element\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Town Map</figcaption></figure>\n<div></div>\n<hr>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\"><b>Town characters</b></span></h3>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/7/75/Scarecrow.png/revision/latest?cb=20150415232632\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Mr Wicker\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Mr Wicker\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"150\" height=\"151\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Mr Wicker</figcaption></figure>\n<p><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/hay-day-8519\" title=\"Hay Day\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Hay Day</a></i>\n</p><p>Mr. Wicker, a talking scarecrow, guides players through the first steps when they unlock the town and later when they unlock the sanctuary.\n</p>\n<div></div>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/c/c6/Lady.png/revision/latest?cb=20191028161453\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"A town visitor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"A town visitor\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>A town visitor</figcaption></figure>\n<p><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/town-visitors-13241\" title=\"Town Visitors\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Town Visitors</a></i>\n</p><p>Ten different <a href=\"/wiki/category%2Fcategory-characters-29468\" title=\"Category:Characters\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">non-player characters</a> come to visit towns and request orders in the different <a href=\"/wiki/service-buildings-24540\" title=\"Service Buildings\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">service buildings</a>.\n</p>\n<div></div>\n<hr>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\"><b>Decorations</b></span></h3>\n<p><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/decorations-6168\" title=\"Decorations\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Decorations</a></i>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/5/54/Sandcastle.png/revision/latest?cb=20150715120116\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Sandcastle decoration\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Sandcastle decoration\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Sandcastle decoration</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Many items can be placed in the town to decorate it, and create paths and fences.\n</p>\n<div></div>\n<hr>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\"><b>Expansion</b></span></h3>\n<p><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/expansion-town-30758\" title=\"Expansion/Town\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Expansion/Town</a></i>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/c/c7/Town-start-separeted-num.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140609035007\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Town area\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Town area\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"150\" height=\"75\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Town area</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Players can expand the town using <a href=\"/wiki/map-piece-13240\" title=\"Map Piece\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Map Pieces</a> and another two of three types expansion materials (land deed, mallet, marker stake) in the farm which can be very occasionally found in the newspaper.\n</p>\n<div></div>\n<hr>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\"><b>Layout Edit Mode</b></span></h3>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/hayday/images/b/b1/Edit_Mode_Icon.png/revision/latest?cb=20160308192446\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Edit Mode button\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Edit Mode button\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"75\" height=\"75\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Edit Mode button</figcaption></figure>\n<p><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/edit-mode-24078\" title=\"Edit Mode\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Edit Mode</a></i>\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/experience-19023\" title=\"Experience\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">experience</a> level&#160;34 onwards, players can use the Layout Edit Mode to edit the current layout of their town and to create new ones.\n</p>\n<div></div>\n<hr>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\"><b>Tutorial</b></span></h3>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\"> <a href=\"/unavailable-source?media=File%3AHay_Day_Town_Introduction_Tutorial\" class=\"video video-thumbnail large\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"> \t<img alt=\"Hay_Day_Town_Introduction_Tutorial\" height=\"280\" width=\"500\" class=\"lazyload\" loading=\"lazy\"> \t<span class=\"thumbnail-play-icon-container\"> \t\t\t</span> </a> <figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<div></div>\n<hr>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\"><b>Strategy tips</b></span></h3>\n<ul><li>There is much more room in the town than on the <a href=\"/wiki/farm-15139\" title=\"Farm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">farm</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/fishing-lake-23340\" title=\"Fishing Lake\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Fishing Lake</a> so expanding the land there is not as critical.</li>\n<li>Town is the BEST way to level up and get <a href=\"/wiki/supplies-23344\" title=\"Supplies\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">supplies</a> in the game by keep serving the visitors and playing regularly.</li>\n<li>Start working on your town as soon as possible. Upgrade your town hall, train station and&#160;all the buildings so that you&#160;can get extra coins, xp, reputation and supplies. If you are active, upgrading the Slots and Time tab is recommended first to multiply your rewards.</li>\n<li>Different service buildings require different goods. The information can be found by searching the service building names in this wiki, so that you can produce more of them.</li>\n<li>You can find a floating chest in the beach occasionally which you can give you different rewards.</li>\n<li>Upgrading the Personal Train requires a lot of refined coal and bars, however, upgrading the time tab is recommended first so that you can pick up townies from your neighborhood friends every 1 hour and 30 min.</li>\n<li>The amount of tools keep increasing with each upgrade you make on the buildings.</li>\n<li>It is really hard to Level Up the reputation in the town. Continuous and Non-Stop playing is preferred to increase your reputation level and upgrade the buildings.</li>\n<li>Reputation level 38 is the last level on which you can finally max your all buildings 100%.</li></ul>\n<hr>\n<p><br>\n</p>\n<table>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td>\n<td>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260901011250\nCache expiry: 1209600\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 878/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 869/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 112/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/200\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.918      1 -total\n 46.85%    5.584      1 Template:Navigation\n 13.26%    1.580      1 Template:Languages\n 11.75%    1.400      1 Template:PageDisplay\n 10.00%    1.192      9 Template:Clr\n  9.71%    1.157      5 Template:Main\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_hayday:pcache:idhash:13129-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timest